        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric M. Plakun\n- Organizations: WAMC, NPR, The New York Times, The Globe and Mail\n- Places: Albany, New York\n- Roles: psychiatrist, psychoanalyst, researcher, forensic psychiatrist\n- Topics: psychotherapy, psychiatry, media appearances\n\nFacts:\n- Eric M. Plakun is an American board certified psychiatrist, psychoanalyst, researcher, and forensic psychiatrist.\n- Eric M. Plakun has been widely published and quoted in the media on psychotherapy and psychiatry, including in The New York Times and The Globe and Mail.\n- Eric M. Plakun has appeared in the media to discuss his psychiatric work on WAMC.\n- WAMC is a public radio network headquartered in Albany, New York, and it is the Albany affiliate of NPR.",
